What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/.../output_enable
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        Inkwell project maintainers
Description:
                Opt-in FRDM i.MX93 EPD bench output lease. Present only with
                inkwell,manual-output-enable on the parallel display formatter.
                That property requires pinctrl states default and gpio to map
                all routed signals to GPIO output-low hogs, and active to map
                them to LCDIF. The legacy default/gpio behavior is unchanged
                when the property is absent.

                Read: 0 = parked, 1 = output lease active. Write 1 to enable
                or renew a two-second lease, only while the DRM encoder is
                active. Write 0 to park immediately. Timeout, DRM disable,
                unbind and orderly host shutdown park the pins and cancel
                the lease. A modeset never automatically restores a lease.
                Timeout is workqueue scheduled, not a hard real-time deadline.

                Root-only writes. The caller must establish logic power and
                exclusive ownership before enabling. This interface neither
                sequences nor measures PMIC rails. It is for panel-disconnected
                electrical tests; it does not implement panel shutdown timing.
